bound-lock/1 about="<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 178\" width=\"640\" height=\"178\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"title desc\">\n<title id=\"title\">A cell</title>\n<desc id=\"desc\">Two origins on one scale: a claims 2 to 9 and b claims 5 to 12; what they hold together runs from a floor of 5 to a ceiling of 9.</desc>\n<style>\ntext{font:14px ui-sans-serif,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fill:#59636e}\n.claim{fill:#8c959f}.held{fill:#2da44e}.pole{fill:#2da44e;font-weight:600}.axis,.tick{stroke:#8c959f;stroke-width:1}.touch{stroke:#2da44e;stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:3 3}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){text{fill:#9198a1}}\n</style>\n<line class=\"touch\" x1=\"269.3\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"269.3\" y2=\"126\"/>\n<line class=\"touch\" x1=\"442.7\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"442.7\" y2=\"126\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"32\" text-anchor=\"end\">a</text>\n<rect class=\"claim\" x=\"139.3\" y=\"18\" width=\"303.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"66\" text-anchor=\"end\">b</text>\n<rect class=\"claim\" x=\"269.3\" y=\"52\" width=\"303.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"end\">held</text>\n<rect class=\"held\" x=\"269.3\" y=\"86\" width=\"173.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<line class=\"axis\" x1=\"96\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"616\" y2=\"126\"/>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"139.3\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"139.3\" y2=\"131\"/>\n<text x=\"139.3\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"269.3\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"269.3\" y2=\"131\"/>\n<text x=\"269.3\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"442.7\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"442.7\" y2=\"131\"/>\n<text x=\"442.7\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"572.7\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"572.7\" y2=\"131\"/>\n<text x=\"572.7\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text>\n<text class=\"pole\" x=\"269.3\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\">floor</text>\n<text class=\"pole\" x=\"442.7\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ceiling</text>\n</svg>\n" at=witness:041/retain-declared-documentation by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/figure shape=docs/img/cell.svg value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 178\" width=\"640\" height=\"178\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"title desc\">\n<title id=\"title\">A cell</title>\n<desc id=\"desc\">Two origins on one scale: a claims 2 to 9 and b claims 5 to 12; what they hold together runs from a floor of 5 to a ceiling of 9.</desc>\n<style>\ntext{font:14px ui-sans-serif,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fill:#59636e}\n.claim{fill:#8c959f}.held{fill:#2da44e}.pole{fill:#2da44e;font-weight:600}.axis,.tick{stroke:#8c959f;stroke-width:1}.touch{stroke:#2da44e;stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:3 3}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){text{fill:#9198a1}}\n</style>\n<line class=\"touch\" x1=\"269.3\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"269.3\" y2=\"126\"/>\n<line class=\"touch\" x1=\"442.7\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"442.7\" y2=\"126\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"32\" text-anchor=\"end\">a</text>\n<rect class=\"claim\" x=\"139.3\" y=\"18\" width=\"303.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"66\" text-anchor=\"end\">b</text>\n<rect class=\"claim\" x=\"269.3\" y=\"52\" width=\"303.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"end\">held</text>\n<rect class=\"held\" x=\"269.3\" y=\"86\" width=\"173.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<line class=\"axis\" x1=\"96\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"616\" y2=\"126\"/>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"139.3\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"139.3\" y2=\"131\"/>\n<text x=\"139.3\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"269.3\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"269.3\" y2=\"131\"/>\n<text x=\"269.3\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"442.7\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"442.7\" y2=\"131\"/>\n<text x=\"442.7\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"572.7\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"572.7\" y2=\"131\"/>\n<text x=\"572.7\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text>\n<text class=\"pole\" x=\"269.3\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\">floor</text>\n<text class=\"pole\" x=\"442.7\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ceiling</text>\n</svg>\n" at=witness:041/retain-declared-documentation by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/ranges-withdrawal shape=docs/img/withdrawal.svg value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 178\" width=\"640\" height=\"178\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"title desc\">\n<title id=\"title\">A cell</title>\n<desc id=\"desc\">Two origins on one scale: seller claims 2 to 9 and buyer claims 5 to 12; what they hold together runs from a floor of 5 to a ceiling of 9.</desc>\n<style>\ntext{font:14px ui-sans-serif,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fill:#59636e}\n.claim{fill:#8c959f}.held{fill:#2da44e}.pole{fill:#2da44e;font-weight:600}.axis,.tick{stroke:#8c959f;stroke-width:1}.touch{stroke:#2da44e;stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:3 3}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){text{fill:#9198a1}}\n</style>\n<line class=\"touch\" x1=\"269.3\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"269.3\" y2=\"126\"/>\n<line class=\"touch\" x1=\"442.7\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"442.7\" y2=\"126\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"32\" text-anchor=\"end\">seller</text>\n<rect class=\"claim\" x=\"139.3\" y=\"18\" width=\"303.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"66\" text-anchor=\"end\">buyer</text>\n<rect class=\"claim\" x=\"269.3\" y=\"52\" width=\"303.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"end\">held</text>\n<rect class=\"held\" x=\"269.3\" y=\"86\" width=\"173.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<line class=\"axis\" x1=\"96\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"616\" y2=\"126\"/>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"139.3\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"139.3\" y2=\"131\"/>\n<text x=\"139.3\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"269.3\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"269.3\" y2=\"131\"/>\n<text x=\"269.3\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"442.7\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"442.7\" y2=\"131\"/>\n<text x=\"442.7\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"572.7\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"572.7\" y2=\"131\"/>\n<text x=\"572.7\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text>\n<text class=\"pole\" x=\"269.3\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\">floor</text>\n<text class=\"pole\" x=\"442.7\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ceiling</text>\n</svg>\n" at=witness:041/retain-declared-documentation by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/ranges-price shape=docs/img/price.svg value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 228\" width=\"640\" height=\"228\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"title desc\">\n<title id=\"title\">A cell</title>\n<desc id=\"desc\">Four origins on one scale: a claims 19.8 to 20.2, b claims 19.9 to 20.3, c claims 19.7 to 20.1 and d claims 24 to 24.4; their claims do not meet.</desc>\n<style>\ntext{font:14px ui-sans-serif,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fill:#59636e}\n.claim{fill:#8c959f}.held{fill:#2da44e}.pole{fill:#2da44e;font-weight:600}.axis,.tick{stroke:#8c959f;stroke-width:1}.touch{stroke:#2da44e;stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:3 3}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){text{fill:#9198a1}}\n</style>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"32\" text-anchor=\"end\">a</text>\n<rect class=\"claim\" x=\"181.4\" y=\"18\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"66\" text-anchor=\"end\">b</text>\n<rect class=\"claim\" x=\"189.1\" y=\"52\" width=\"31.1\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"end\">c</text>\n<rect class=\"claim\" x=\"173.6\" y=\"86\" width=\"31.1\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"end\">d</text>\n<rect class=\"claim\" x=\"507.3\" y=\"120\" width=\"31.1\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"end\">held</text>\n<text x=\"96\" y=\"168\">their claims do not meet</text>\n<line class=\"axis\" x1=\"96\" y1=\"194\" x2=\"616\" y2=\"194\"/>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"173.6\" y1=\"194\" x2=\"173.6\" y2=\"199\"/>\n<text x=\"173.6\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\">19.7</text>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"204.7\" y1=\"194\" x2=\"204.7\" y2=\"199\"/>\n<text x=\"204.7\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20.1</text>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"507.3\" y1=\"194\" x2=\"507.3\" y2=\"199\"/>\n<text x=\"507.3\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\">24</text>\n<line class=\"tick\" x1=\"538.4\" y1=\"194\" x2=\"538.4\" y2=\"199\"/>\n<text x=\"538.4\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\">24.4</text>\n</svg>\n" at=witness:041/retain-declared-documentation by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/ranges-thermometer shape=docs/img/thermometer.svg value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="A cell is drawn as bars on one scale: a grey bar is what one origin claims, potential until another meets it, and a green bar is where two claims meet, its ends the floor and the ceiling. A state carries its render in a figure, a badge and a graph alike: FREE green, REQUIRED grey, FORBIDDEN red, CONFLICT fork." at=witness:the-root-spoke-for-the-place by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/marks value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="A cell" at=witness:the-root-spoke-for-the-place by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/cell/title value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="A new tree ratio requires its own handed leaf and region population with a digest and native capture. The old population does not constrain a new place. Empty regions falsify the universal inequality." at=witness:descriptive-measures-beside-states by=target form=interval measure=count needs=observation/T58/handed-population role=demands scope=observation/T58/cardinality value=0..0
bound-lock/1 about="Binary M0 with jointly independent Bernoulli(p) latent lineages, known p in(0,1), uniform shares1/K with K>=1 and0<c<=1: the exact population pair and fourth agreement moments identify(c,K). A general quartic expectation bridge and strict monotonicity prove this beyond the old finite grid. For arbitrary normalized weights, p declared is insufficient for this moment map: c=7/10,K_eff=147/4 and c=4/5,K_eff=48 have equal R2,R4 at p=3/4. This collision concerns these moments only, not the entire observable law. R3 remains redundant. No sample uncertainty, causal recovery or contextual activity identification is claimed." at=witness:obligations046/m0-identification by=target form=interval measure=count needs=proofs/m0-046-identification/M0Identification046.lean|proofs/m0-046-identification/Obligations045/M0Coincidence.lean|proofs/m0-046-identification/lake-manifest.json|proofs/m0-046-identification/lakefile.toml|proofs/m0-046-identification/lean-toolchain|vectors/laws/m0-identification.lean.json|contracts/m0-moment-identification.json|samples/laws/m0-moment-identification/yes/sample.json|samples/laws/m0-moment-identification/no/sample.json|vectors/laws/policy.json role=demands scope=publication/evidence/m0-identification value=0..0
bound-lock/1 about="Binary M0 with jointly independent Bernoulli(p) latent lineages, known p in(0,1), uniform shares1/K with K>=1 and0<c<=1: the exact population pair and fourth agreement moments identify(c,K). A general quartic expectation bridge and strict monotonicity prove this beyond the old finite grid. For arbitrary normalized weights, p declared is insufficient for this moment map: c=7/10,K_eff=147/4 and c=4/5,K_eff=48 have equal R2,R4 at p=3/4. This collision concerns these moments only, not the entire observable law. R3 remains redundant. No sample uncertainty, causal recovery or contextual activity identification is claimed.\n" at=witness:obligations046/O4 by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/m0-moment-identification shape=docs/contracts/m0-moment-identification.md value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Bounded diagnostic contract: on a finite acyclic rest graph with its exact reverse-edge index, bites traverses travelling non-widening ceiling marks and stops below an envelope a when meet(a,new)=a. Descendant travelling envelopes contain that ancestor meet and are also absorbed. Its cells and visits describe this diagnostic traversal. With no local widening, local-only ceiling constraints or claim spans masking these envelopes, the fixture matches changed ceilings. It proves neither actual propagation cost nor a general region-summary interval. Historical alias: a-signature-stops-where-the-meet-is-identity." at=policy:law/T94 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T94-a-signature-stops-where-the-meet-is-identity.json|samples/no/T94-a-signature-stops-where-the-meet-is-identity.json|src/field/sign.ts|src/lattice/obligatory.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T94-a-signature-stops-where-the-meet-is-identity value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Bounded enumeration contract: for a finite cell history and fixed finite acyclic world with total lattice operations, fragility enumerates subsets of distinct live origin names in increasing size. For each subset it removes all history records by those names and compares both poles. It returns the smallest size changing a pole, or sentinel0 if no tested subset does. This is history-record deletion, not automatic phased cancellation; cross-origin takes can expose old records. Simultaneous-support intuition additionally assumes no cross-origin withdrawal dependencies and no masking marks. Historical alias: fragility-is-the-fewest-withdrawals." at=policy:law/T101 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T101-fragility-is-the-fewest-withdrawals.json|samples/no/T101-fragility-is-the-fewest-withdrawals.json|src/field/fragility.ts|src/lattice/obligatory.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T101-fragility-is-the-fewest-withdrawals value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Bounded interval-budget contract: in a finite acyclic world with inhabited poles, finite ceiling/floor endpoints and no local widening, pay explicitly appends a travelling ceiling mark at hi-1. It refuses if hi-1<floor.lo; otherwise looksLeft decreases by one with the rest of the snapshot unchanged. The caller must explicitly charge a look; sign, observe and refine are not thereby charged automatically. Region membership is computed by the existing region predicate. No universal physical price, policy optimality or third-object claim follows. Historical alias: every-act-is-paid-by-its-origin." at=policy:law/T93 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T93-every-act-is-paid-by-its-origin.json|samples/no/T93-every-act-is-paid-by-its-origin.json|src/debit/observer.ts|src/field/sign.ts|src/lattice/obligatory.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T93-every-act-is-paid-by-its-origin value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Bounded object contract: with an unchanged acyclic world, well-formed unique claim ids and a withdrawal naming only the newly appended claim, observe followed by that named withdrawal restores the earlier live claims and hence its poles. The earlier state is restored, not necessarily grey. Separately, equal-magnitude opposite-signed phasors at the same phase modulo a declared positive period cancel. Epoch or causal labels alone are not phase equality. Historical alias: withdrawal-is-an-anti-claim." at=policy:law/T85 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T85-withdrawal-is-an-anti-claim.json|samples/no/T85-withdrawal-is-an-anti-claim.json|src/field/observe.ts|src/lattice/obligatory.ts|src/views/field/wave.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T85-withdrawal-is-an-anti-claim value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Bounded storage/read contract: sign and require append one mark at the named cell and retain ancestor records. On finite acyclic snapshots with unique ids and no widening, poles fold applicable live local and travelling-ancestor marks and live local claims by meets; the result is independent of replay order of the same records. Withdrawing a uniquely named tighter mark exposes the meet of the remaining marks, which may include an absorbed earlier signature. One appended record is not a runtime-cost theorem: map copying and ancestry traversal are separate, and a DAG read is not bounded by depth alone. Historical alias: signatures-live-where-they-are-signed." at=policy:law/T95 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T95-signatures-live-where-they-are-signed.json|samples/no/T95-signatures-live-where-they-are-signed.json|src/field/sign.ts|src/field/require.ts|src/lattice/obligatory.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T95-signatures-live-where-they-are-signed value=present
bound-lock/1 about="CI stages, the owner promotes with 2FA: one origin is potential, the second makes information" at=policy:publish/staged-1 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=pipeline/publish/command value="npm stage publish"
bound-lock/1 about="Candidate marginal information measure on one finite declared rational joint prior: Delta=I(truth;new source|previous sources)=H(truth|previous)-H(truth|previous,new). Both addition orders retain identical full data and prior. The existing conditional-loss measure supplies the entropy terms. Source lineage labels do not enter the calculation; no truth-free estimation or public export is added." at=policy:measure/marginal-information by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=proofs/marginal-information.json|src/measures/marginal-information.ts|samples/laws/marginal-information/yes.json|samples/laws/marginal-information/no.json|vectors/laws/marginal-information.json role=demands scope=measure/marginal-information value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Candidate oracle pair measure: on an explicit complete T-cell frame and theta, score is the same wrong response rate, obtained from the published truth-conditioned coincidenceExcess. No truth means unmeasured. Above-threshold components are descriptive; recovering a handed partition requires max outside < theta < min inside, plus finite-sample premises for confidence. No causal group is identified." at=policy:measure/cofailure-oracle by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=proofs/cofailure-pairs.json|src/measures/cofailure-pairs.ts|samples/laws/cofailure-pairs/yes.json|samples/laws/cofailure-pairs/no.json|vectors/laws/cofailure-pairs.json role=demands scope=measure/cofailure-pairs-oracle value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Candidate oracle-free measure: same response rate minus the fixed handed independent-categorical reference sum_v q_i(v)q_j(v). No truth is read; a missing reference is unmeasured. Shared questions can give positive excess without shared errors. This is a different observable from published coincidenceExcess; neither a lineage cause, c nor correctness is identified." at=policy:measure/cofailure-without-truth by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=proofs/cofailure-pairs.json|src/measures/cofailure-pairs.ts|samples/laws/cofailure-pairs/yes.json|samples/laws/cofailure-pairs/no.json|vectors/laws/cofailure-pairs.json role=demands scope=measure/cofailure-pairs-without-truth value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Checks finite Lean Helly evidence, the existing H1 sample and explicit diagnostic countertables, and an enumerated declared unanimity mixture through the published fitter; no universal product law or causal identification." at=witness:044/public-case-layout by=target form=interval measure=count needs=proofs/helly-comb.json|proofs/resolution-encounters.json|proofs/coordination.json|proofs/lean/Obligations/HellyComb.lean|vectors/laws/helly-comb.lean.json|samples/laws/linage-rest/yes/sample.json|samples/laws/linage-rest/no/sample.json|samples/yes/H1-uncertainty.json|samples/no/H1-uncertainty.json|vectors/laws/policy.json|vectors/laws/helly-comb.json|vectors/laws/resolution-encounters.json|vectors/laws/coordination.json role=demands scope=publication/evidence/linage-rest value=0..0
