bound-lock/1 about="Clone, `{check}`. A case that gives you a different answer is the contribution: send it with what it printed.\n{open} conjectures are open, each in the README under Open, and each says what would close it and who could.\nNothing else is asked. Lines land through the fold, never by hand; a page and the lock disagree, the lock is right." at=witness:the-root-spoke-for-the-place by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contributing value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Coincidence excess compares a declared null; a positive excess does not identify a common cause." at=witness:041/cleanup-models-and-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=rationale/041/reference-not-cause value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Conditional comparison only: given the same previous tuple S, if truth -> (S,Y_other) -> Y_same, then I(truth;Y_same|S)<=I(truth;Y_other|S). Exact-copy redundancy is a special case; strict gain needs positive conditional information. Equal individual accuracy or information, or distinct lineage labels, does not establish this hypothesis. The standard Shannon argument is cited, not newly Lean-formalized; finite vectors retain reversals, saturation, XOR synergy and majority loss." at=policy:law/marginal-comparison by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=proofs/marginal-information.json|vectors/laws/marginal-information.json restsOn=measure/marginal-information role=demands scope=law/marginal-conditional-comparison value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Conditional consequence of data processing: uniform truth X passes through an n-ary symmetric channel X->Z of declared crossover c, all reports depend on X only through Z, and aggregate A depends only on reports. Then I(X;A)<=capacityP0(n,c)=log2(n)-h2(c)-c*log2(n-1). The expression is already published at private p=0; neither a cause frequency nor marginal error alone establishes this channel. F1 separately bounds the partition residual RI_H on a uniform N-element universe; it does not bound designated-truth information. Finite vectors and counterexamples are captured; the general Shannon argument is cited, not Lean-formalized; admission remains open." at=policy:law/lineage-markov by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=proofs/lineage-ceiling.json|samples/laws/lineage-ceiling/yes.json|samples/laws/lineage-ceiling/no.json|vectors/laws/lineage-ceiling.json role=demands scope=law/lineage-symmetric-markov-ceiling value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Count explicitly pending native file-closure checks in the two clean installed consumers. Zero only after all compiled bytes, exports, tests and actual native checks match. A failed, interrupted, stale, malformed or incompatible capture refuses. File closure does not authorize release; the unchanged 0..0 bound selects the measured result." at=witness:041/installed-closure-reading by=target form=interval measure=count needs=samples/yes/installed-artifact.json|samples/no/installed-artifact.json|vectors/measures/installed-artifact.cli.json|package.json|dist/ role=reads scope=release/installed-artifact value=0..0
bound-lock/1 about="Covariance and its spectrum describe binary error indicators, not joint reported values or independence." at=witness:041/cleanup-models-and-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=rationale/041/spectrum-proxy value=lock
