bound-lock/1 about="F1 bounds RI_H=I(U;V|G) for partitions on a finite uniform N-atom universe; the conditional lineage ceiling bounds I(X;aggregate) for a designated truth and declared channel. Their units are bits but their objects and cardinalities differ. Neither expression is a substitute for the other. Existing F1 path evidence is reused." at=policy:law/lineage-F1-boundary by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=proofs/lineage-ceiling.json|vectors/laws/lineage-ceiling.json|vectors/laws/f1/path-witness.json restsOn=law/thm-extremal|law/lineage-symmetric-markov-ceiling role=demands scope=law/lineage-F1-object-boundary value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Finite law by enumeration: K=1..4, p=11/20..19/20, c=1/20..20/20, uniform shares. All 720 closed scores equal exact binary-configuration enumeration and lie in [0,1]. This is a static score formula, not a proof of the N-limit. The false WF expected-floor monotonicity is rejected by a normalized 21-state counterexample at N=5,p=3/4,c=9/10,w=(3,1,1)/5.\n" at=witness:obligations045 by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/m0-finite-grid shape=docs/contracts/m0-finite-grid.md value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Finite named X, exact rational mu_X>=0 summing to1; total deterministic maps Y=f(X), Z=g(Y); mu_Y=f_*mu_X and mu_Z=g_*mu_Y, never separately chosen priors. Zero-mass fibers contribute0. Units bits. H_mu(X|Z)=H_mu(X|Y)+H_mu(Y|Z). Loss vanishes exactly when the respective projection is injective on positive support. No independence assumption. All partitions of four named atoms, every nested coarsening, all nonnegative integer masses summing4 divided4. Binary64 log2 tolerance1e-12. This is bounded enumeration, not a universal kernel proof. General Lean proof and native admission remain pending." at=witness:obligations046/projection-chain by=target form=interval measure=count needs=vectors/laws/projection-chain.native.json|contracts/projection-chain.json|proofs/projection-chain.md|vectors/laws/policy.json|vectors/laws/projection-chain.json|samples/laws/projection-chain/yes/sample.json|samples/laws/projection-chain/no/sample.json role=demands scope=publication/evidence/projection-chain value=0..0
bound-lock/1 about="Finite named X, exact rational mu_X>=0 summing to1; total deterministic maps Y=f(X), Z=g(Y); mu_Y=f_*mu_X and mu_Z=g_*mu_Y, never separately chosen priors. Zero-mass fibers contribute0. Units bits. H_mu(X|Z)=H_mu(X|Y)+H_mu(Y|Z). Loss vanishes exactly when the respective projection is injective on positive support. No independence assumption. All partitions of four named atoms, every nested coarsening, all nonnegative integer masses summing4 divided4. Binary64 log2 tolerance1e-12. This is bounded enumeration, not a universal kernel proof. General Lean proof and native admission remain pending.\n" at=witness:obligations046/O7 by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/projection-chain shape=docs/contracts/projection-chain.md value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Finite nonconvex Helly counterexample, kernel checked in Lean: subsets {0,1}, {1,2}, {0,2} meet pairwise with witnesses 1,0,2 while their triple meet is empty. This does not alter the interval-only T38 or claim failure for convex intervals." at=policy:law/helly-comb by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=proofs/helly-comb.json|proofs/lean/Obligations/HellyComb.lean|vectors/laws/helly-comb.lean.json|vectors/laws/helly-comb.json role=demands scope=law/helly-comb value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Finite refutation under the published binary M0 static floor functional: p=3/4,c=9/10,neutral Wright-Fisher N=5,initial named counts(3,1,1). All21 multinomial descendant count states,including zero shares,have total probability1. The initial floor32/128=1/4 exceeds E[next floor]=92440/(128*3125)=2311/10000 by189/10000. Reuses the unchanged published Obligations045.wf_transition_normalized and wf_floor_decreases_in_expectation certificates. This refutes universal expected-floor nondecrease; it does not assert universal decrease or a new probability-limit theorem. The floor-monotone-in-t claim is refuted and its closed-lineage-law roadmap alias remains withdrawn; conditional lineage capacity is unaffected.\n" at=witness:obligations046/O3 by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/m0-wf-floor-refutation shape=docs/contracts/m0-wf-floor-refutation.md value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Finite refutation under the same declared M0 p=3/4,c=9/10: named weights(1,4,4)/9 and(2,2,5)/9 both have sum(w_l^2)=11/27 and K_eff=27/11,while their static floors are5/32 and1/4. Reuses the unchanged published Obligations045.same_effective_participation_different_floor certificate. Therefore K_eff alone does not determine this floor even with p,c fixed. This does not refute the distinct pair-coincidence identity and supplies no identification or uncertainty guarantee.\n" at=witness:obligations046/O3 by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/m0-keff-floor-refutation shape=docs/contracts/m0-keff-floor-refutation.md value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="For a finite nonempty family of nonempty closed real intervals, pairwise nonempty intersection implies a nonempty total intersection. The lattice interval form supplies this finite Helly-2 case; no polygon/consensus claim for arbitrary forms. Convex families in R^d require Helly hypotheses and d+1 witnesses; discrete circle and halfplane fixtures distinguish pairs from triples. Historical alias: origins-are-a-polygon." at=policy:law/T38 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/laws/t38/intervals.json|vectors/laws/t38/circle12.json|vectors/laws/t38/halfplanes.json|test/t38-forms.test.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T38-origins-are-a-polygon value=present
bound-lock/1 about="For a finite nonempty set of uniformly weighted admissible states at a fixed resolution, freedom is log2 of its cardinality, equal to its Shannon entropy. A narrowing act cannot increase this quantity. Withdrawal and witnessed local join can increase it on an existing object; phase and vacuity experiments do not establish that these are the only possible changes. Historical alias: freedom-is-entropy." at=policy:law/T90 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T90-freedom-is-entropy.json|samples/no/T90-freedom-is-entropy.json|test/laws-boundaries-042.test.ts|vectors/laws/a7-t90.json restsOn=law/D4-debit-in-bits|law/A7-freedom-conserved role=demands scope=law/T90-freedom-is-entropy value=present
bound-lock/1 about="For a finite nonempty set of uniformly weighted admissible states at fixed resolution, debit is log2 of its cardinality. A singleton has zero debit. An empty set has no uniform distribution; any zero-debit convention for empty/vacuous regions is separate from this Shannon statement." at=policy:law/D4 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=samples/yes/D4-debit-in-bits.json|vectors/freedom.json|vectors/debits.json|test/laws-boundaries-042.test.ts|vectors/laws/a7-t90.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A3-resolution role=demands scope=law/D4-debit-in-bits value=present
bound-lock/1 about="For a finite world with finite records, an acyclic dependency order and total supplied lattice operations, ancestry expansion visits each reachable name once and parts/meet perform finitely many operations. This is finite evaluation, not convergence of an arbitrary monotone-map iteration. Monotonicity alone allows a two-cycle from incomparable seeds. Every reachable dependency cycle is rejected; unreachable cycles do not affect the query. Arbitrary iterative convergence remains open without operator, seed and progress hypotheses. Historical alias: the-fold-is-total." at=policy:law/T99 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T99-the-fold-is-total.json|samples/no/T99-the-fold-is-total.json|test/fold-boundaries-042.test.ts|vectors/laws/a9-t99.json|src/lattice/obligatory.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T99-the-fold-is-total value=present
bound-lock/1 about="For a fixed family of supplied lattice values, associative and commutative meet is independent of their arrival permutation. This does not erase effective epochs, widening, withdrawals or the order of equal-epoch acts." at=policy:law/A2 by=target form=alphabet kind=axiom measure=status needs=samples/yes/A2-meet.json|samples/no/A2-meet.json|vectors/meet.json|vectors/join.json|vectors/fold.json|test/knowledge-laws-042.test.ts role=demands scope=law/A2-meet value=present
bound-lock/1 about="For a fixed nonempty finite world with unique coordinates, neighbours forms the undirected graph of shared supplied origins, excluding explicitly named bounds. On each connected component distance is shortest-path length: reversing paths proves symmetry, concatenating paths proves the triangle inequality, and zero length identifies one vertex. Breadth-first layers return the minimum path length. The implementation returns world.length as the top sentinel for an unreachable pair; it is not an observed travel length. Sample means and any physical interpretation remain experiments." at=policy:law/T41 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings.json|src/views/product/reach.ts|test/wave.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A5-origin-is-extension role=demands scope=law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings value=present
bound-lock/1 about="For a fixed supplied collection of signed bounds with declared polarity and lattice form, foldSigned retains the extensional classes and evaluates their form operations; meet of fixed permit values is associative and commutative. This static fold is not a claim that chronological withdrawal, replacement or witnessed widening can never occur." at=policy:law/T19 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T19-signatures-fold.json|vectors/signatures.json restsOn=law/A2-meet|law/D7-fork role=demands scope=law/T19-signatures-fold value=present
bound-lock/1 about="For finite distinct real walls and finite distinct sites strictly inside their bounding consecutive-wall intervals, grow assigns each site the interval between its wall or nearest-site midpoints. Adding another distinct interior site while retaining the walls cannot increase an existing site width: its left endpoint can only increase and its right endpoint can only decrease. No encounter, sufficient-resolution or general-form growth law follows; wall-coincident, duplicate, nonfinite and out-of-domain sites are outside this claim." at=policy:law/T39 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T39-cells-grow-until-stopped.json|src/views/product/reach.ts|test/wave.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier role=demands scope=law/T39-cells-grow-until-stopped value=present
bound-lock/1 about="For finite held real intervals and lock intervals with strictly positive finite width, stretching about each fixed midpoint eventually contains every bounded nonempty held interval; an empty held interval is never accepted by red. pour counts reached named lock places. tense interpolates touched inhabited endpoints toward their held endpoints at a handed rate in [0,1]; touching narrows width only when the held interval is no wider, and may widen it otherwise. Missing or empty observations use the specified widening rule. The historical seeded deformation counts are experiments, not a physical adaptation law." at=policy:law/T37 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T37-a-lock-is-a-mould.json|src/views/product/mould.ts|test/loom.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T37-a-lock-is-a-mould value=present
bound-lock/1 about="For fixed coordinates, resolution, context and signed ceilings, adding live narrowing claims cannot increase the sum of log-cardinalities of finite admissible states. Exact withdrawal and witnessed local widening may reopen freedom at the same coordinate. The blanket exclusivity claim that only a new coordinate raises freedom is not valid. Historical alias: freedom-conserved." at=policy:law/A7 by=target form=alphabet kind=axiom measure=status needs=samples/yes/A7-freedom-conserved.json|samples/no/A7-freedom-conserved.json|test/laws-boundaries-042.test.ts|vectors/laws/a7-t90.json role=demands scope=law/A7-freedom-conserved value=present
bound-lock/1 about="For the actual M0 product law, moving-threshold majority and fair-tie transfer are conditional on standardized fixed-cut CDF convergence to F, continuous at zero. The tie atom then vanishes; conditionalError tends to F(0), hence to one half only when F(0)=1/2 is declared. The actual M0 CLT remains unpaid and open. A scalar LGN limit alone does not give half error." at=witness:obligations046/m0-diagonal-threshold by=target form=interval measure=count needs=proofs/m0-046-diagonal/BridgeNegatives.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Bridge.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Diagonal046.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Lindeberg046.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Moments046.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Threshold046.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/ConsensusGrid.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Coincidence.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Diagonal.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Limit.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Offdiag.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/lake-manifest.json|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/lakefile.toml|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/lean-toolchain|vectors/laws/m0-diagonal-threshold.lean.json|contracts/m0-diagonal-conditional.json|samples/laws/m0-diagonal-conditional/yes/sample.json|samples/laws/m0-diagonal-conditional/no/sample.json|vectors/laws/policy.json role=demands scope=publication/evidence/m0-diagonal-conditional/threshold value=0..0
bound-lock/1 about="For the actual M0 product law, moving-threshold majority and fair-tie transfer are conditional on standardized fixed-cut CDF convergence to F, continuous at zero. The tie atom then vanishes; conditionalError tends to F(0), hence to one half only when F(0)=1/2 is declared. The actual M0 CLT remains unpaid and open. A scalar LGN limit alone does not give half error.\n" at=witness:obligations046/m0-diagonal-threshold by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/m0-diagonal-threshold shape=docs/contracts/m0-diagonal-threshold.md value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="For the declared binary M1 ancestor-first fixed-quota model, the complete finite generative PMF contains jointly independent named ancestor and leaf correctness bits and three independent primitive bits per member: ancestor selector, conditional leaf selector, and fresh vote. Summing unused primitive draws gives exclusive masses c1, (1-c1)c2, (1-c1)(1-c2)p and (1-c1)(1-c2)(1-p). Pushing this law to named lineage counts yields the product binomial law with q_l=c1 A_parent(l)+(1-c1)c2 B_l+(1-c1)(1-c2)p. For every finite N its fair-majority error is exactly the finite latent mixture of binomial errors. This identity is compiled in Lean without assuming a count law or convergence theorem. It does not prove an asymptotic floor, a CLT, a calibrated public API or causal identification." at=witness:obligations046/m1-generator-binomial by=target form=interval measure=count needs=proofs/m1-046-bridge/M0Bridge.lean|proofs/m1-046-bridge/M1Bridge046.lean|proofs/m1-046-bridge/Obligations045/M0Limit.lean|proofs/m1-046-bridge/Obligations045/M0Offdiag.lean|proofs/m1-046-bridge/lake-manifest.json|proofs/m1-046-bridge/lakefile.toml|proofs/m1-046-bridge/lean-toolchain|vectors/laws/m1-generator-binomial.lean.json|contracts/m1-subcauses.json|contracts/m1-generator-binomial.json|samples/laws/m1-generator-binomial/yes/sample.json|samples/laws/m1-generator-binomial/no/sample.json|vectors/laws/policy.json role=demands scope=publication/evidence/m1-generator-binomial value=0..0
bound-lock/1 about="For the declared binary M1 ancestor-first fixed-quota model, the complete finite generative PMF contains jointly independent named ancestor and leaf correctness bits and three independent primitive bits per member: ancestor selector, conditional leaf selector, and fresh vote. Summing unused primitive draws gives exclusive masses c1, (1-c1)c2, (1-c1)(1-c2)p and (1-c1)(1-c2)(1-p). Pushing this law to named lineage counts yields the product binomial law with q_l=c1 A_parent(l)+(1-c1)c2 B_l+(1-c1)(1-c2)p. For every finite N its fair-majority error is exactly the finite latent mixture of binomial errors. This identity is compiled in Lean without assuming a count law or convergence theorem. It does not prove an asymptotic floor, a CLT, a calibrated public API or causal identification.\n" at=witness:obligations046/O6-bridge by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/m1-generator-binomial shape=docs/contracts/m1-generator-binomial.md value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="For the declared finite binary M1 ancestor-first fixed-quota model, if every named ancestor/leaf latent configuration has score S different from1/2, the actual full-generator fair-majority error tends to the exact latent threshold functional sum_z mass(z)1{S(z)<1/2}. The proof uses the admitted finite primitive-generator/binomial bridge, prefix-quota convergence, the exact finite conditional second moment and variance at mostN/4. For any fixed epsilon>0, once the finite conditional mean divided byN lies on the correct side with margin epsilon, its error gap is at most1/(4N epsilon^2). This yields the off-diagonal limit without an assumed probability limit, ambient process oracle or CLT. A concrete shared-parent two-leaf example withp=2/3,c1=c2=1/2 meets the off-diagonal condition. Configurations onS=1/2, causal identification and calibration are outside this theorem; the three original research cards remain open." at=witness:obligations046/m1-offdiag-limit by=target form=interval measure=count needs=proofs/m1-046-offdiag/M0Bridge.lean|proofs/m1-046-offdiag/M0Diagonal046.lean|proofs/m1-046-offdiag/M0Moments046.lean|proofs/m1-046-offdiag/M1Bridge046.lean|proofs/m1-046-offdiag/M1Offdiag046.lean|proofs/m1-046-offdiag/Obligations045/M0Limit.lean|proofs/m1-046-offdiag/Obligations045/M0Offdiag.lean|proofs/m1-046-offdiag/lake-manifest.json|proofs/m1-046-offdiag/lakefile.toml|proofs/m1-046-offdiag/lean-toolchain|vectors/laws/m1-offdiag-limit.lean.json|contracts/m1-subcauses.json|contracts/m1-offdiag-limit.json|samples/laws/m1-offdiag-limit/yes/sample.json|samples/laws/m1-offdiag-limit/no/sample.json|vectors/laws/policy.json role=demands scope=publication/evidence/m1-offdiag-limit value=0..0
bound-lock/1 about="For the declared finite binary M1 ancestor-first fixed-quota model, if every named ancestor/leaf latent configuration has score S different from1/2, the actual full-generator fair-majority error tends to the exact latent threshold functional sum_z mass(z)1{S(z)<1/2}. The proof uses the admitted finite primitive-generator/binomial bridge, prefix-quota convergence, the exact finite conditional second moment and variance at mostN/4. For any fixed epsilon>0, once the finite conditional mean divided byN lies on the correct side with margin epsilon, its error gap is at most1/(4N epsilon^2). This yields the off-diagonal limit without an assumed probability limit, ambient process oracle or CLT. A concrete shared-parent two-leaf example withp=2/3,c1=c2=1/2 meets the off-diagonal condition. Configurations onS=1/2, causal identification and calibration are outside this theorem; the three original research cards remain open.\n" at=witness:obligations046/O6-offdiag by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/m1-offdiag-limit shape=docs/contracts/m1-offdiag-limit.md value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="For the declared member product, c<1 and the published quota rule imply positive growing actual variance. For each epsilon>0 the member-level Lindeberg truncated-second-moment ratio is eventually exactly zero. At epsilon=0 it equals one for N>0. This is a checked CLT hypothesis, not a CLT theorem." at=witness:obligations046/m0-diagonal-lindeberg by=target form=interval measure=count needs=proofs/m0-046-diagonal/BridgeNegatives.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Bridge.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Diagonal046.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Lindeberg046.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Moments046.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Threshold046.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/ConsensusGrid.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Coincidence.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Diagonal.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Limit.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Offdiag.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/lake-manifest.json|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/lakefile.toml|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/lean-toolchain|vectors/laws/m0-diagonal-lindeberg.lean.json|contracts/m0-diagonal-conditional.json|samples/laws/m0-diagonal-conditional/yes/sample.json|samples/laws/m0-diagonal-conditional/no/sample.json|vectors/laws/policy.json role=demands scope=publication/evidence/m0-diagonal-conditional/lindeberg value=0..0
bound-lock/1 about="For the declared member product, c<1 and the published quota rule imply positive growing actual variance. For each epsilon>0 the member-level Lindeberg truncated-second-moment ratio is eventually exactly zero. At epsilon=0 it equals one for N>0. This is a checked CLT hypothesis, not a CLT theorem.\n" at=witness:obligations046/m0-diagonal-lindeberg by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/m0-diagonal-lindeberg shape=docs/contracts/m0-diagonal-lindeberg.md value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="For the existing object state reading with fewer than two distinct live origin names, the cell cannot be FREE: incompatible required/signed constraints give CONFLICT first, otherwise the origin-count branch gives REQUIRED. Further claims of the same origin do not increase that distinct-name count. The seeded twenty-cell play results are experiments; player permissions, identity authenticity, independence, asymmetric economic value and an unsuspendable referee are not consequences of this state rule and remain open." at=policy:law/T57 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T57-a-refereed-game-governs-itself.json|src/lattice/obligatory.ts|src/field/encounter.ts|src/views/field/policy.ts|test/obligatory.test.ts restsOn=law/A8-four-states|law/D11-the-obligatory role=demands scope=law/T57-a-refereed-game-governs-itself value=present
bound-lock/1 about="For two unit complex amplitudes with real phases, let delta=acos(cos(a-b)) in [0,pi]. Then |exp(ia)+exp(ib)|^2=2+2*cos(delta), and it is below 2 iff delta>pi/2. Raw absolute phase difference is not invariant under full turns. Laminarity, fork/close ratios and the F4 worst-case objective are not conclusions of this identity. Historical alias: the-quarter-turn." at=policy:law/T87 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T87-the-quarter-turn.json|samples/no/T87-the-quarter-turn.json|test/measures/t87-phase.test.ts|src/views/field/wave.ts|src/field/encounter.ts role=demands scope=law/T87-the-quarter-turn value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Formal Lean witness for the existing A2 interval instance under LinearOrder: endpoint meet is associative, commutative and idempotent, and narrows in the published API preorder. Raw empty pairs remain distinct; observable interval meanings form a meet semilattice. Replay consequences concern fixed accumulated restrictions only, not withdrawal, widening, epochs, provenance erasure or authority. Lean compilation and finite published-JavaScript correspondence are captured; Bound admission remains open." at=policy:law/A2-interval-lean by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=proofs/lean/Obligations/Cell.lean|proofs/lean/Obligations/Bridge.lean|proofs/lean/lean-toolchain|proofs/lean/lakefile.toml|proofs/lean/lake-manifest.json|vectors/laws/meet-semilattice.json|samples/laws/semilattice/yes.json|samples/laws/semilattice/no.json|src/lattice/forms.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/A2-interval-semilattice-lean value=present
bound-lock/1 about="H1 remains open: the published resolution and encounters sample supplies neither a counting/refinement model nor definitions of K and N. A rising product does not refute a lower bound. Diagnostic tables refute monotonicity from increasing resolution alone and unqualified K,N bounds. No independent-origin inference is made." at=policy:research/resolution-encounters by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=proofs/resolution-encounters.json|vectors/laws/resolution-encounters.json role=demands scope=research/resolution-encounters value=present
bound-lock/1 about="How to read it" at=witness:the-root-spoke-for-the-place by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/reading/heading value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="In a common probability space with justified declared failure upper bounds p_i, the probability of all declared events succeeding is at least max(0,1-sum(p_i)); sum(p_i)>=1 is trivial. Agreement and copy counts do not estimate probabilities. Historical alias: freedom-is-a-currency; no transferability or unforgeability claim." at=policy:law/T18 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/measures/confidence/union-bound.json|vectors/measures/confidence/expected.json role=demands scope=law/T18-freedom-is-a-currency value=present
bound-lock/1 about="In a finite undirected graph with distinct named vertices, positive component sizes and unrestricted unit-cost fresh bridges that join only their two chosen components, a nonnegative integer budget b minimises unreachable unordered pairs by connecting the min(b+1,k) largest of k components into one. The objective is (N^2-sum(componentSize^2))/2; arbitrary site restrictions, nonuniform costs and origin-name collisions are outside this theorem. design returns a star on representatives of those components. Historical comparisons against particular blind seeds remain experiments, not universal superiority over every competing draw." at=policy:law/T51 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T51-the-shape-of-knowing-can-be-designed.json|src/views/product/design.ts|src/views/product/reach.ts|test/obligatory.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A5-origin-is-extension role=demands scope=law/T51-the-shape-of-knowing-can-be-designed value=present
bound-lock/1 about="In the declared binary M1 ancestor-first fixed-quota model, a latent configuration with every q_i=1/2 has fair-majority error exactly1/2 at every finiteN. Thus the complete implementation and primitive-generator mixture converge to the latent threshold functional whenever every latent configuration is either off diagonal or entirely unbiased. A two-level example p=3/4,c1=1/5,c2=1/6,one ancestor and one leaf has a positive-mass unbiased diagonal state and a Lean-proved full-generator error limit1/32. For heterogeneous diagonal configurations, positive fresh massd=(1-c1)(1-c2) gives variance>=N*d^2*p*(1-p), bounded quota drift, vanishing standardized threshold and the checked bounded-array Lindeberg condition for epsilon>0. These are prerequisites, not a proved general CLT. Transfer from actual primitive fixed-cut CDF limits to the moving majority cut is proved only with that distributional convergence supplied explicitly. The general heterogeneous-diagonal probability limit remains open, as do the three original research cards." at=witness:obligations046/m1-diagonal-partial by=target form=interval measure=count needs=proofs/m1-046-diagonal/M0Bridge.lean|proofs/m1-046-diagonal/M0Diagonal046.lean|proofs/m1-046-diagonal/M0Lindeberg046.lean|proofs/m1-046-diagonal/M0Moments046.lean|proofs/m1-046-diagonal/M0Threshold046.lean|proofs/m1-046-diagonal/M1Bridge046.lean|proofs/m1-046-diagonal/M1Diagonal046.lean|proofs/m1-046-diagonal/M1Offdiag046.lean|proofs/m1-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Limit.lean|proofs/m1-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Offdiag.lean|proofs/m1-046-diagonal/lake-manifest.json|proofs/m1-046-diagonal/lakefile.toml|proofs/m1-046-diagonal/lean-toolchain|vectors/laws/m1-diagonal-partial.lean.json|contracts/m1-subcauses.json|contracts/m1-diagonal-regions.json|samples/laws/m1-diagonal-regions/yes/sample.json|samples/laws/m1-diagonal-regions/no/sample.json|vectors/laws/policy.json role=demands scope=publication/evidence/m1-diagonal-partial value=0..0
bound-lock/1 about="In the declared binary M1 ancestor-first fixed-quota model, a latent configuration with every q_i=1/2 has fair-majority error exactly1/2 at every finiteN. Thus the complete implementation and primitive-generator mixture converge to the latent threshold functional whenever every latent configuration is either off diagonal or entirely unbiased. A two-level example p=3/4,c1=1/5,c2=1/6,one ancestor and one leaf has a positive-mass unbiased diagonal state and a Lean-proved full-generator error limit1/32. For heterogeneous diagonal configurations, positive fresh massd=(1-c1)(1-c2) gives variance>=N*d^2*p*(1-p), bounded quota drift, vanishing standardized threshold and the checked bounded-array Lindeberg condition for epsilon>0. These are prerequisites, not a proved general CLT. Transfer from actual primitive fixed-cut CDF limits to the moving majority cut is proved only with that distributional convergence supplied explicitly. The general heterogeneous-diagonal probability limit remains open, as do the three original research cards.\n" at=witness:obligations046/O6-diagonal by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/m1-diagonal-regions shape=docs/contracts/m1-diagonal-regions.md value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="L7: conditional bound on one declared common probability space: P(N>k)<=min(1,sum over |S|=k+1 of min p_i), with rational declared marginal failure upper bounds and 0<=k<=m. Trivial iff computed upper bound is one. Counterexamples refute the former top-k+1 success guarantee. Joint-independent Bernoulli convolution is a separate declared hypothesis; rho=0 and pairwise independence do not supply it. Existing stronger 0.4.2 count bound is unchanged and needs no joint independence." at=policy:law/L7 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=samples/measures/l7-tolerant-k.json|vectors/laws/l7-tolerant-k.json|vectors/laws/policy.json restsOn=law/T18-freedom-is-a-currency role=demands scope=law/L7-tolerant-k value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="L8: law by enumeration only for 3<=n<=64, positive integer divisors p|n and integer 0<=s<p. D=log2(n/p)-h(s/p), explicit binary64-log2 approximation. Odd-period minimum uses h(floor(p/2)/p), even-period minimum uses one. Complete maximum at zero; nonzero domain has endpoints 1,p-1, empty when p=1. No information or worst-case interpretation follows from nonnegativity. T87 retains its separate wrapped-phase amplitude identity." at=policy:law/L8 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=samples/measures/l8-phase-defect.json|vectors/laws/l8-phase-defect.json|vectors/laws/policy.json role=demands scope=law/L8-F4-integer-phase-defect value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="L9: law by counterexample of existence of noninjective weighted mix, and measure with a declared prior on a finite explicitly supplied set of named-factor configurations. Equal-weight ab and ba give the same bottom tie and different named forks. Loss is H(configuration | mix)=H(configuration)-H(mix); a uniform prior must be explicitly selected, absent prior is unmeasured. The four-state uniform example has mean loss 0.5 bits and one bit conditioned on tie; the injective named fork has zero loss. Defines no new algebraic act, governance selection, M/3 or M/4 law, or destroyed field." at=policy:law/L9 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=samples/measures/l9-mix-loss.json|vectors/laws/l9-mix-loss.json|vectors/laws/policy.json role=demands scope=law/L9-mix-projection-loss value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="Learn from an example: {pages}" at=witness:the-root-spoke-for-the-place by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/pointers/learn value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="M/3 is the only admitted conditional model. Superseded descriptive D/commonMass claims are retired; observed commonMass remains descriptive, never strength or independence." at=witness:descriptive-measures-beside-states by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=rationale/040/model-text value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="M0 conditional law: normalized joint product probabilities of named individual Bernoulli outcomes push forward to the exact product-binomial count law. conditional_error_representation and model_mixture_error_representation identify that finite PMF fair-majority expectation and its normalized latent mixture with the existing conditionalError and error for every N. ambient_conditional_error_representation transfers from measurable raw-bit snapshots with that declared joint product law; no binomial count law, expected-error equality or convergence is assumed. fair_loss_average_bridge requires N>0; conditional_error_zero and zero_average_counterexample distinguish N=0. computational_offdiag_limit composes the exact representation with the existing floor_limit_offdiag_mixture theorem under its stated integrability, independence, identical-distribution, mean and measurability assumptions, plus every latent score unequal to 1/2. Domain: finite fixed K, normalized nonnegative fixed weights, p in (1/2,1), c in [0,1), published cumulative-floor allocation and fair ties. Pairwise independence alone is insufficient, certified by pairwise_not_joint. General diagonal, c=1, moment identification, root admission and release readiness are not claimed.\n" at=witness:obligations046/m0-binomial-bridge by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/m0-binomial-bridge shape=docs/contracts/m0-binomial-bridge.md value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="M0 with the published c<1 domain and cumulative-floor quotas. Every conditional q_i=1/2 implies exact conditionalError=1/2 for every N, including zero. A diagonal score alone does not imply every q_i=1/2. General heterogeneous diagonal remains open; c=1 is excluded and parity distinguishes its failure." at=witness:obligations046/m0-diagonal-symmetric by=target form=interval measure=count needs=proofs/m0-046-diagonal/BridgeNegatives.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Bridge.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Diagonal046.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Lindeberg046.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Moments046.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/M0Threshold046.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/ConsensusGrid.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Coincidence.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Diagonal.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Limit.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/Obligations045/M0Offdiag.lean|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/lake-manifest.json|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/lakefile.toml|proofs/m0-046-diagonal/lean-toolchain|vectors/laws/m0-diagonal-symmetric.lean.json|contracts/m0-diagonal-conditional.json|samples/laws/m0-diagonal-conditional/yes/sample.json|samples/laws/m0-diagonal-conditional/no/sample.json|vectors/laws/policy.json role=demands scope=publication/evidence/m0-diagonal-conditional/symmetric value=0..0
bound-lock/1 about="M0 with the published c<1 domain and cumulative-floor quotas. Every conditional q_i=1/2 implies exact conditionalError=1/2 for every N, including zero. A diagonal score alone does not imply every q_i=1/2. General heterogeneous diagonal remains open; c=1 is excluded and parity distinguishes its failure.\n" at=witness:obligations046/m0-diagonal-symmetric by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/m0-diagonal-symmetric shape=docs/contracts/m0-diagonal-symmetric.md value=lock
