bound-lock/1 about="Named experiment: object.test.ts simulates300 independent finite interval cells,20 explicit looks per epoch,64 states per initial cell, expiry after10 epochs and200 epochs. A running signed price ledger telescopes so freedom left plus the ledger equals its initial value; the captured fixture reports steady1200 under this scheduler. That bookkeeping identity is not Shannon entropy conservation, and the finite fixture does not prove general convergence, physical attention cost or an entropy-flow claim. Historical alias: an-act-is-paid-with-attention." at=policy:law/T100 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T100-an-act-is-paid-with-attention.json|samples/no/T100-an-act-is-paid-with-attention.json|src/debit/observer.ts|test/object.test.ts role=demands scope=law/T100-an-act-is-paid-with-attention value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Named phase-assignment experiment: the existing fixture chooses the withdrawal epoch equal to the observation epoch when rests=false, and uses the declared withdrawal epoch when rests=true. That chosen convention yields its measured phasors, but neither-rests-on-the-other does not itself prove phase equality. A dependent withdrawal one full period later also cancels; unrelated claims assigned different phases need not. Any general concurrency-if-and-only-if-cancellation theorem requires a declared cross-clock phase-comparison rule and remains open. Historical alias: concurrent-withdrawal-cancels." at=policy:law/T104 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T104-concurrent-withdrawal-cancels.json|samples/no/T104-concurrent-withdrawal-cancels.json|test/object.test.ts|src/views/field/wave.ts role=demands scope=law/T104-concurrent-withdrawal-cancels value=present
