bound-lock/1 about="Reduction to a discrete join — Every pair with trivial meet can be transformed, without decreasing $\\RI_H$ and in finitely many steps, into a pair on the same $n$ states with trivial meet and discrete join." at=policy:law/lem-join by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/lem-join.json|test/f1-boundary-042.test.ts|vectors/laws/f1/path-witness.json restsOn=law/lem-identity role=demands scope=law/lem-join value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Reduction to a trivial meet — Let $\\tau(N)$ denote the maximum of $\\RI_H$ over pairs on $N$ states with trivial meet. Then for any $x,y\\in\\Pin$ with $x\\wedge y$ having blocks of sizes $n_1,\\dots,n_r$, \\[ \\RI_H(x,y)=\\sum_{t=1}^{r}\\frac{n_t}{n}\\,\\RI_H\\bigl(x|_{B_t},y|_{B_t}\\bigr) \\;\\le\\;\\sum_t \\frac{n_t}{n}\\,\\tau(n_t). \\] Each restricted pair has trivial meet. If $\\tau$ is non-decreasing the bound is $\\tau(n)$; and if $\\tau$ is moreover strictly increasing above $N=2$, equality for $n\\ge3$ forces $r=1$." at=policy:law/lem-meet by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/lem-meet.json|test/f1-boundary-042.test.ts|vectors/laws/f1/path-witness.json restsOn=law/lem-identity|law/prop-cmi role=demands scope=law/lem-meet value=present
