bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment, one-origin structural interpretation; general/physical-law reading open. amplitudes with a phase and no origin, no signed ceiling, no resolution and no epoch band are what is left of a cell when those four fields are dropped, so the measurement problem is the absence of who, imposed symmetries the absence of a signed ceiling, the classical limit the absence of resolution and universal interference the absence of bands; restored, four claims in phase keep exactly the share of the whole their number leaves them against an environment spread over the period, and six origins around one value are six objects read finely and one read coarsely, so how many things there are is a reading; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=policy:law/H5 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H5-hilbert-is-the-obligatory-without-four-fields.json|samples/no/H5-hilbert-is-the-obligatory-without-four-fields.json restsOn=law/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move|law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase|law/T36-agreement-has-a-resolution|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled role=demands scope=law/H5-hilbert-is-the-obligatory-without-four-fields value=present
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment, one-origin structural interpretation; general/physical-law reading open. stated as a hint and never as a claim about the world: if what is is a field of floors and ceilings, a distant signature changes a cell whose own record never moved, and in two hundred trials of one cell holding one value the verdict came out both ways, so nothing stored at the cell explains the difference and what explains it is the bound the cell rests on; the resemblance is structural and never arithmetic, with no continuous amplitudes and no inequality violated by number; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=policy:law/H3 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move.json|samples/no/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move.json restsOn=law/T46-a-bound-moves-cells-no-walk-reaches|law/T47-a-two-pole-object role=demands scope=law/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move value=present
