bound-lock/1 about="cf. — $\\RI_H(x,y)=I(x;y\\mid x\\wedge y)$. Domain: two partitions of a nonempty finite uniformly weighted universe. Let Z be their common coarsening, a function of both X and Y. The entropy chain rule gives I(X;Y|Z)=H(X)+H(Y)-H(X,Y)-H(Z), which is the declared residual-information expression. This is a partition identity, not a causal-independence inference." at=policy:law/prop-cmi by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/prop-cmi.json|test/laws-papers.test.ts|test/f1-boundary-042.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A2-meet|law/D5-declaration role=demands scope=law/prop-cmi value=present
